\ Plain generic dispatch on bare metal: method hits on two builtin types, two
\ default-body misses, and a binary method, printed through the UART-backed
\ output stream. The boolean operand's type never appears in the runtime image,
\ so it exercises the wildcard-only lookup path.

describe: generic ( x -- s ) [ drop "unknown" ] ;
describe: method{ fixnum } [ drop "a fixnum" ] ;
describe: method{ string } [ drop "a string" ] ;

combine: generic ( a b -- s ) [ drop drop "mixed" ] ;
combine: method{ fixnum fixnum } [ drop drop "two fixnums" ] ;

42 describe print-line
"hello" describe print-line
t describe print-line
1 2 combine print-line
"x" 3 combine print-line

\ Protocol- and combinator-bounded dispatch on bare metal: a call site whose
\ parameter is bounded by a protocol emits the satisfies-and-dispatch helper,
\ and one bounded by an intersection emits the combinator variant. fixnum
\ implements both protocols' methods, so both bounds are satisfied and both
\ helpers dispatch positively.

labeled: protocol{ label: } ;
sized: protocol{ size-class: } ;

label: generic ( x: labeled -- s ) [ drop "unlabeled" ] ;
label: method{ fixnum } [ drop "labeled fixnum" ] ;

size-class: generic ( x: labeled & sized -- s ) [ drop "unsized" ] ;
size-class: method{ fixnum } [ drop "sized fixnum" ] ;

7 label print-line
7 size-class print-line
